The code statements that lead to the bug are:
<text>
ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, pruss_of_free_clk_provider,
                               clk_mux_np);
if (ret) {
    dev_err(dev, "failed to add clkmux free action %d", ret);
    goto put_clk_mux_np;
}
</text>
Reason:
On failure, devm_add_action_or_reset() already calls pruss_of_free_clk_provider() which does of_node_put(clk_mux_np). Then the error path jumps to `put_clk_mux_np` which calls of_node_put(clk_mux_np) again, causing a double free (use-after-free).

The code statements that fix the bug are:
<text>
ret = devm_add_action_or_reset(dev, pruss_of_free_clk_provider,
                               clk_mux_np);
if (ret)
    dev_err(dev, "failed to add clkmux free action %d", ret);
return ret;
</text>
Reason:
By removing the `goto put_clk_mux_np` and returning directly after the error message, the duplicate of_node_put() at the `put_clk_mux_np` label is avoided. The return value `ret` is now correctly propagated, and the function exits without an extra node put.

